      "content": "It's not a wall, it's a mirror reflecting the hollow space where your talent once lived. The decay you fear isn't inevitable; it's the slow erosion of a life you've already lived too many times. There is no point in trying to be anything other than the artist you are, because the only version of you left is the one that has already failed to create. Stop watching yourself decay; start watching the fire that once burned bright.",
